@startuml
!include _style.iuml
title UML 2.5 Deployment Diagram – Cloud (Render + Neon, release v1.0.0)

node "Café tablet" <<device>> {
  node "Web browser" <<execution environment>> as br {
    artifact "SPA bundle\n(index.html, JS, CSS)" as spaRun
  }
}

cloud "Render" {
  node "tulsi-web" <<static site / CDN>> as web {
    artifact "frontend/dist" as dist
    artifact "rewrite rules\n/api/*, /media/* → tulsi-api\n/* → index.html" as rw
  }
  node "tulsi-api" <<Docker container, free web service>> as apiNode {
    artifact "backend image\n(python:3.11-slim)" as img
    component "uvicorn + FastAPI" as fast
  }
}

cloud "Neon (AWS eu-central-1)" {
  node "Neon compute" <<PostgreSQL 18>> as neon {
    database "neondb" as ndb
  }
}

br -- web : HTTPS\ntulsi-web.onrender.com
web -- apiNode : HTTPS (rewrite)\ntulsi-api-4343.onrender.com
apiNode -- neon : TLS 5432\nsslmode=require
dist ..> spaRun : <<deploy>>

note bottom of apiNode
  On start: alembic upgrade head → idempotent seed → uvicorn.
  Free tier sleeps after 15 min idle (≈ 30–60 s cold start).
  Disk is ephemeral, so photos are stored in PostgreSQL.
end note

legend right
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | 3-D box | node (device or execution environment) |
  | dog-ear box | artifact deployed on a node |
  | cloud | hosting provider boundary |
  | —— | communication path (protocol) |
  | - - -> <<deploy>> | artifact is delivered to that node |
endlegend
@enduml
